 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Keep it in the fridge or in the freezer. If you going out for the day, wrap it in blanket and put it in a cold spot. Ice cubes melt faster than blocks, so go for the block. Pack it in soft clothes so it doesn't scratch the container. Don't pack it too tight. Air needs to move around it, so leave some space. Teach him to leave it alone and put his own food in fridge. Or keep weekend icebox in a separate room. Yes, pour hot water over the block in the morning and again before bed. It lasts longer than you' think.",
